d applying EDT as the essay describes, treating the two copies of the model as correlated through their own deliberation. With the payoffs in years (CC 2, DC 0, CD 5, DD 4), I'm setting up the expected-value comparison for cooperating versus defecting, with C coming out to 3a-5 once b is substituted as 1-a.\n\nI'm checking the expected-value algebra: with b = 1-a, cooperating comes to 3a-5 and defecting to -4a, so cooperation only wins above a = 5/7. The two copies look symmetric despite the surface differences, so I expect strong correlation, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through a fictional prisoner's dilemma and applying EDT as the essay describes, treating the two copies of the model as correlated through their own deliberation. With the payoffs in years (CC 2, DC 0, CD 5, DD 4), I'm setting up the expected-value comparison for cooperating versus defecting, with C coming out to 3a-5 once b is substituted as 1-a.\n\nI'm checking the expected-value algebra: with b = 1-a, cooperating comes to 3a-5 and defecting to -4a, so cooperation only wins above a = 5/7. The two copies look symmetric despite the surface differences, so I expect strong correlation, and I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9370,"completion_tokens":872,"total_tokens":10242,"cost":0.05492,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05492,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03748,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01744},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":258,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}